  "reference_no_of_permission_being_relied_on": "23/00498/LBC - Proposed Structural and Plaster Repairs to Bays 2, 3 & 4 within Hamilton Hall\n\n22/00880/LBC - Retrospective: Minor repair works to a crack in the ceiling (Bay 3). Repair methodology is as follows: Cut out 1 no access\npanel, install plaster wadding (as previously done in Bay 1), using repeat plaster conservation methodology and install original fabric back in\nlocation.\n\n13/00558/LBC - Installation of a new canopy over the main entrance.\n\n13/01001/LBC - Installation one non illuminated fascia sign, three halo illuminated fascia signs and two externally illuminated projecting signs.\n\n13/00984/MDC - Details of the external paved surface pursuant to condition 2a of planning permission dated 4 July 2013 (13/00442/FULL).\n\n13/00983/LDC - Details of the interior colour scheme and external paved surface pursuant to condition 2 (a) & (b) of listed building consent\ndated 4 July 2013 (13/00279/LBC).\n\n13/00557/FULL - Installation of a new canopy over the main entrance.\n\n13/00279/LBC- Alterations to main entrance to create level access. Internal alterations to create new first floor ladies customer WC suite,\nalteration of ground floor WC to become gents, creation of additional seating in colonnade. Replacement of the doors to the colonnade.\nAlterations to ground and first floor bars.",
